'' RUN: std/process phase P5 -- argument round trip (spaces, quotes, backslashes before quotes,
'' trailing backslashes, empty, tab, non-ASCII incl. a surrogate pair) checked against the OS's own
'' CommandLineToArgvW in the child; ToString; Run/Shell exit codes; Capture with 1 MiB on both pipes
'' (no deadlock) and StderrToStdout; stdinData echo; a Child's PipeStreams through fs.Stream; Env /
'' EnvRemove / EnvClear; NUL and '=' refused; Cwd and a bad Cwd; PATH lookup in the child's PATH and
'' never in the current directory; a .cmd through cmd.exe and '%PATH%' refused; HANDLE_LIST keeping an
'' inheritable legacy OPEN handle out; TryWait / WaitTimeout / Kill; and std/os's cross-process tests
'' (C:\dev\docs\tiko-stdlib\RFC-0001 sections 8.6 and 9.3): os.Args with non-ASCII and embedded
'' quotes, and a child in its own process group sent CTRL_BREAK_EVENT reporting INT_BREAK through its
'' exit code.  The same source runs on Linux in WSL (SIGKILL, SIGTERM -> INT_TERMINATE).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/std-process-p5.tiko -o tests/codegen/stdprocp5.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/stdprocp5.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/stdprocp5.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
